Description: Forget the pending registration reply once it is processed.
 This is a follow-up to the fix for #234: without it, deactivate_bus() cancels a pending call which was freed already.
Author: Mike Gorse <mgorse@suse.com>
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/at-spi2-core/-/commit/ce75b1ffd379a5d179107f984e11cd68cf621f9f
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/at-spi2-core/-/issues/240
Applied-Upstream: 2.60.6
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
diff --git a/atk-adaptor/bridge.c b/atk-adaptor/bridge.c
index 7e1ba694..e732ceba 100644
--- a/atk-adaptor/bridge.c
+++ b/atk-adaptor/bridge.c
@@ -341,6 +341,8 @@ register_reply (DBusPendingCall *pending, void *user_data)
   DBusMessage *reply;
   SpiBridge *app = user_data;
 
+  app->register_pending = NULL;
+
   reply = dbus_pending_call_steal_reply (pending);
   dbus_pending_call_unref (pending);
 
